WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:05.263
- [Interviewer] All right.

00:00:05.263 --> 00:00:06.620
Robert? - Mmm hmm.

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:07.453
- [Interviewer] Robert,
where'd you grow up?

00:00:07.453 --> 00:00:08.286
Where are you from originally?

00:00:08.286 --> 00:00:13.140
- I'm from New York, Harlem,
New York city, 116 2nd Avenue.

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:14.120
- [Interviewer] Tell me
about your childhood.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.210
You had both your parents growing up?

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:18.280
- Yeah, for a little while
because my father used to beat up

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.860
on my mom all the time and stuff.

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:23.130
So as a kid, I used to
always put my sisters

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:25.623
in their room so they don't
have to go through it.

00:00:27.199 --> 00:00:30.970
(groans) Every time he
would hit her and stuff

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:32.580
I would like try to get
in the middle and stuff

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:33.780
so he would hit me and stuff.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:36.690
Then I will tell him,
mom, dad, why are you,

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:37.890
Papi, why are you hitting her?

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:38.723
You know?

00:00:38.723 --> 00:00:39.833
And he wouldn't answer me.

00:00:39.833 --> 00:00:42.230
"Get out of here", you know,
smack me and stuff like that,

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:43.870
you know, but he would lock her

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:46.730
in the room and started throw
ashtrays on her, you know?

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:48.330
And I always get in the front

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:51.220
of him and stuff, try to,
you know, stop it and stuff.

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:53.850
But I was just a little boy, you know.

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.230
I couldn't do much and stuff.

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:56.063
You know,

00:00:56.063 --> 00:00:58.400
I couldn't understand why he
was hitting her all the time.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:59.233
- [Interviewer] Your mom?

00:00:59.233 --> 00:01:00.860
- Yeah, my mom and so,

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:01.840
and come to realize

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:03.910
after a whole lot of
years later, you know,

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:06.520
it was because he was jealous
of her career and stuff.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.750
My mom came over here with, at age 18

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:10.300
from Puerto Rico, you know,

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:11.950
and made something to herself, you know.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:13.877
She worked hard and she always told me:

00:01:13.877 --> 00:01:17.090
"You want to be somebody
in life, get an education."

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:18.450
And she went to college and all that.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:21.213
She made something of herself,
you know, she be good.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:25.180
I'm always, always a
good person, but you know

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:30.830
Ooh, excuse me. (sniffles)

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:33.023
When I was about five years old and stuff,

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:36.407
I was molested from my babysitter,

00:01:36.407 --> 00:01:37.240
(traffic passes) you know

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:39.690
cause my father was
always drunk, you know?

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:41.830
So it was like my mom would
have to pay somebody else

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:44.909
to watch us and stuff,
you know, after school.

00:01:44.909 --> 00:01:47.470
(sighs heavily)

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:49.900
Excuse me. (engine revs)

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:51.467
Oh, man.

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:55.440
You know, but I was, I was
molested by my babysitter.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:57.650
You know after that and my
mom couldn't take it no more,

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:59.720
and she, and we left, we left my father

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:01.240
in the apartment all by himself
(brakes squeal) and stuff.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:02.690
You know, we had to escape

00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:04.770
through the fire escape (brakes
squeal) to get away from him

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:05.680
'cause he wouldn't let us through,

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:07.470
out through the door, (brakes
squeal) the front door.

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:09.140
So we had to escape through a fire escape.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:10.870
You know, I remember it well.

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:13.120
I had to take my sisters down one

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:16.950
by one and stuff and I'm a
little boy, but you know, I just

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.649
I did whatever when my
mom told me to, you know?

00:02:19.649 --> 00:02:22.280
What little boy want to see
his mom get hit, you know?

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:26.983
You know, but anyway we
moved to another apartment

00:02:26.983 --> 00:02:29.190
(sniffles softly) and my mom, you know,

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:30.640
she knew that I was going through a lot,

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:33.149
so she put me into sports
and stuff, you know

00:02:33.149 --> 00:02:36.210
(sniffles) to try to
get me, get me, you know

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:38.740
my mind away from that
and stuff, you know?

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:41.750
And I, I became real
good at sports and stuff,

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.360
but, (traffic passes) I don't know.

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:45.850
I always had it.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:47.420
I would try to hold everything inside

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:49.950
until I would explode,
you know? (horn honks)

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:53.430
And then come to find
out my oldest sister,

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:55.900
my father tried to rape
her on the roof, you know?

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:58.070
And I didn't know about this, you know?

00:02:58.070 --> 00:02:59.800
His own brother beat the fuck out of him

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:00.920
when he found out what happened.

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:03.460
And so, you know, my mom took my sister

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:04.890
and sent her to Puerto Rico and stuff.

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:06.370
You know, 'til everything was cleared

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:07.760
out and stuff, you know.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:08.980
I dunno whatever happened

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:10.540
about that case and stuff, you know?

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:14.070
But my own uncle man, beat the
hell out my father, you know?

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:16.770
And just like, man
tried to rape my sister?

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:20.437
What's wrong with you, you
know, but I don't get it, man.

00:03:20.437 --> 00:03:21.270
You know?

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:24.030
And I always respected him, but I just,

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:26.360
I couldn't do what he wanted to do.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:29.740
It wasn't no father, you know,
like I knew he was my father

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:32.690
but, it's like, I have no love and respect

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:34.940
for him because of what he
did and stuff, you know?

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:37.000
I don't want to be like that all my life.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:40.040
I tried to like, don't
hit no women, you know.

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:42.610
I wouldn't do nothing like
that and stuff, you know.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:45.950
It's, I don't want to be
nothing like him, you know?

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.720
But I started messing up.

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:50.960
You know, I started doing,
turning toward drugs and stuff.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:53.530
You know, just doing stupid shit.

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:56.280
Crime, committing crimes
and stuff, you know?

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:58.090
So that way (traffic passes)
I'm not in my head all the time

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:02.050
'cause my head man, oh man,
it's something else, you know?

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:04.000
- [Interviewer] How
far'd you go in school?

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.210
- I went through to ninth
grade and I was supposed to go

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:10.260
to high school, but me
trying to be a player

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:13.010
or whatever you want
to call it, stupid ass,

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:16.330
you know, I started dating
cousins and all that,

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:17.910
and they chased me out of school

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:19.720
with bats and stuff, you know,

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:22.760
'cause I was dating the same
cousins and stuff, you know?

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:24.640
So I dropped out of school, you know

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:27.470
and my mom always said, "If
you're not going to school,

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:28.740
you gotta get a job."

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:29.573
You know?

00:04:29.573 --> 00:04:30.406
So that's what I did.

00:04:30.406 --> 00:04:32.740
I got a job, and I
started working, you know.

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:35.080
My mom was the one that
got me my first job

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:36.330
when I was seven years old,

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:38.710
working at the best fruit stand, you know,

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:40.470
that was beautiful.

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:42.217
You know, cause she
always told me, you know,

00:04:42.217 --> 00:04:43.558
"I'll get you what you need,

00:04:43.558 --> 00:04:46.230
but if you want something, you
gotta do that on your own."

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:47.350
And I respected that.

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:49.510
You know, my mom always
had good jobs, you know

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:51.240
'cause she had a college degree.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:54.870
You know, she was a nurse, you know,

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:57.230
and from there she became a cop.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.603
I was so proud of her.

00:04:58.603 --> 00:05:01.420
Man, she came out on the
newspaper and the front page

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:03.500
and all that and the Puerto Rican parade.

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:05.100
It was beautiful, you know,

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:07.400
and I got like a hundred
newspapers and stuff, you know

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:08.700
with her picture on there.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:11.190
You know, 'cause I was proud
of my mother, you know.

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:12.500
She always been like my mother

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:14.570
and my friend, my best friend, you know?

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:16.380
And she always told me
the truth, you know?

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:18.550
No matter what happens is to just call me

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:19.710
and I'll come get you,

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:22.590
and she was the only one
that ever kept her word.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:25.670
Everybody else was just like,
they lied to me, you know?

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:28.440
So it's like, I grew up
with a lot of hatred,

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:30.660
you know, anger, I don't
know, (bird chirps)

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.727
just, I couldn't understand
it and stuff, you know,

00:05:32.727 --> 00:05:34.343
but my mom always tried to like,

00:05:35.263 --> 00:05:37.230
tried to put me in school and all that.

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:40.349
You know, I just recently,
like maybe four years ago,

00:05:40.349 --> 00:05:41.182
(bird chirps)

00:05:41.182 --> 00:05:44.230
I went back to school and I
got my GED diploma, you know?

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:46.060
And I dedicated that to my mom.

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:48.570
Cause she was always trying
to get me to, (engine revs)

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:50.410
you know, get my education and all that.

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:52.420
She said, "If you want
to be somebody in life,

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:54.130
you have to get an education."

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:56.130
You can always get a job and then that,

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:58.777
but if you want a career
and people respect you,

00:05:58.777 --> 00:06:00.830
get an education, you know?

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:03.833
And I believe that, you know,
but I was so stupid, you know,

00:06:03.833 --> 00:06:06.951
like always went into one ear
and out the other, you know,

00:06:06.951 --> 00:06:09.910
(birds chirp) and now
it's like my baby sis,

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:12.010
my baby sister passed away from cancer.

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:13.270
That hurt me a whole lot.

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:15.290
I was always close to her, you know?

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:18.770
And I tried throwing my father
out the window, you know?

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:21.600
And if it wasn't for my
cousin, I would have succeeded.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:24.960
You know, because it's
just, you know, my sister,

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:27.660
she died of cancer and you know, she had

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:29.270
she gave birth to my nephew and stuff,

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:32.490
and six months later they
found out that she had cancer

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:33.330
but it was too late (birds chirp)

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:34.650
to do anything about it and stuff.

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:37.040
It's already went to her
stomach and all that.

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:39.995
Man, it was hard to see my
sister go like that, you know?

00:06:39.995 --> 00:06:44.310
But, I guess it's a reason for
everything in life, you know?

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:47.730
And it's like, oh man, (air
brakes hiss) ever since then,

00:06:47.730 --> 00:06:51.370
if I just have been on one, I don't know.

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:53.550
I do good for a little while
(birds chirp) and then I get

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:57.466
into my head, and it's, I
messed everything up and stuff.

00:06:57.466 --> 00:06:58.930
(horn honks) Every time I was doing good

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:01.420
and stuff like that, I always
find a reason to mess it up.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:04.520
And I don't know why I keep
doing that, but it's like

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.530
I just started going to therapy and stuff

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:09.440
and I'm trying to get all these feelings

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:10.790
and emotions out of me and stuff,

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:12.550
'cause I still have all that inside of me,

00:07:12.550 --> 00:07:14.630
and every time I think about it and I cry

00:07:14.630 --> 00:07:16.180
and I have all this anger and stuff,

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:17.720
'cause I never let it out

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:20.777
and I always held
everything inside, you know?

00:07:20.777 --> 00:07:22.860
And I don't want to take
it out on the wrong person

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:25.100
or do something stupid and get me

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:27.210
in jail for the rest of my life.

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:29.127
You know, I've been in and out of jail,

00:07:29.127 --> 00:07:31.320
for the, like the last 30 years, man.

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:32.620
I'm tired of that.

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:34.030
I'm seriously tired. (birds chirp)

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:36.087
I just want to do
something to help people,

00:07:36.087 --> 00:07:40.330
and you know, the last
time I was in jail was 2013

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:41.677
and I asked The Lord,

00:07:41.677 --> 00:07:43.547
"Man, please help me stay out of jail."

00:07:43.547 --> 00:07:45.810
"Help me to become a
good person and stuff."

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:48.663
I had no idea it was going
to get me a heart, you know?

00:07:48.663 --> 00:07:50.560
I ain't never felt nothing in life

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:53.030
'cause I didn't want to, you know, I mean,

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:54.550
you know everything I
went through and stuff,

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:57.070
I was like, for what I'm doing this for?

00:07:57.070 --> 00:08:00.140
For what reason and stuff, it's
just gonna end up the same?

00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:02.430
You know, I didn't trust no man.

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:05.540
And my stepfather, he came into our life

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:07.990
like maybe two years
after we left my father

00:08:07.990 --> 00:08:10.110
and I didn't even trust him and stuff.

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:11.030
And he was good.

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:11.970
He was good to us.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:14.920
All he ever wanted, was a family, a son.

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:17.140
And so, cause he couldn't have no kids.

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:18.395
You know, (truck beeps)

00:08:18.395 --> 00:08:20.560
and he was so proud to
say I'm his son, you know?

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:23.390
And since I didn't trust nobody and stuff,

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:25.651
I couldn't like, love
him the way I wanted to,

00:08:25.651 --> 00:08:26.550
(brakes squeal) you know?

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:28.370
And he did a lot for us.

00:08:28.370 --> 00:08:30.470
You know, but I never, I just

00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:32.370
I don't know if I didn't appreciate it

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:34.469
or it just, I was just scared, you know?

00:08:34.469 --> 00:08:35.302
(traffic passes loudly)

00:08:35.302 --> 00:08:38.510
But I think about it
now, and I felt so bad,

00:08:38.510 --> 00:08:40.650
for all the things I've
done to him, you know?

00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:43.960
I mean, I've done, I hit him, you know?

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:47.890
I pushed, as a little boy I put
cigarette butts in his beer,

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:49.770
you know, but it's,

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:51.370
I guess I was trying to push him away,

00:08:51.370 --> 00:08:54.240
so he don't hurt my mother, you know?

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:57.820
And it's like, man, and coming
out to think about it now,

00:08:57.820 --> 00:09:00.750
all that man ever tried to do was love us.

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:01.650
You know what I mean?

00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:03.713
It's like, and I was pushing 'em away.

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:05.811
I don't know for what reason.

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:10.811
I just, you know, and he
passed away from cancer too.

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.909
So then my mom passed away, of cancer.

00:09:14.909 --> 00:09:16.880
A lot of people in my family passed away

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:18.877
from either cancer or
cirrhosis of the liver,

00:09:18.877 --> 00:09:21.590
and stuff like that, you know?

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:23.790
I've been to a lot of funerals

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:26.020
and I'm just tired (bird
chirps) of going through it.

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:29.150
Then my last couple of
girlfriends, they ended up,

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:32.080
after I get with them, it's
like they will all die on me

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:32.913
or something.

00:09:32.913 --> 00:09:34.610
I don't know why.

00:09:34.610 --> 00:09:35.443
I already had,

00:09:35.443 --> 00:09:38.620
I already had maybe, like
four girlfriends, you know?

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:40.640
It's like, I'm tired of it, man.

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:41.540
I try.

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:45.740
I mean, when my sister was in
the hospital dying of cancer,

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:46.717
I asked the Lord and said,

00:09:46.717 --> 00:09:49.077
"Why are you taking her
for, she's so good?"

00:09:49.077 --> 00:09:51.210
"Why don't you take me, you
know, I'm the one that's messed

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:52.280
up in my head and stuff."

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:53.860
I just, but I couldn't understand it.

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:56.580
I didn't understand, The
Lord, when The Lord wants you,

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:58.107
he gonna get you, you know?

00:09:58.107 --> 00:10:00.010
And you have to believe in that, you know,

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:03.000
you have to believe in
something in life, you know?

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:06.900
So it's like, man, I'm
surprised, I'll be 52 next month,

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:07.810
and I,

00:10:07.810 --> 00:10:10.120
I ain't think I'll make it to pass 25.

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:11.780
You know, because of the way I was living.

00:10:11.780 --> 00:10:13.973
I didn't wanna live, you know?

00:10:15.987 --> 00:10:18.500
Going through that in life, man, it's man,

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:20.657
it messes you up, you know?

00:10:20.657 --> 00:10:22.930
And I'm trying to get back, you know?

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:24.110
I'm trying to be good.

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:26.020
You know, I don't do all the
things that I used to do,

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:29.490
like rob people and sell drugs, and,

00:10:29.490 --> 00:10:31.940
I don't commit no crime,
not even jaywalking.

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:32.773
I'm too scared,

00:10:32.773 --> 00:10:34.340
'cause I don't want to
go back to prison man.

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:36.357
You know, I'm tired of that, man.

00:10:36.357 --> 00:10:37.720
I don't want to do that.

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:39.470
I don't want to be a bad person

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:42.250
but I didn't think he would
give me a heart, you know?

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:43.580
I actually cried today.

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:45.010
You know, I actually do things

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:47.882
