asked was (traffic passes)

00:10:52.570 --> 00:10:55.550
for me to get it, to stay
out of prison, that's all.

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:57.480
That's all I want, man, do good.

00:10:57.480 --> 00:10:59.010
Help somebody.

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:01.020
You know, I didn't think
he would give me a heart

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:01.853
like this though.

00:11:01.853 --> 00:11:04.890
I mean, I help everybody, even
though they steal from me,

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:09.569
and you know, just do bad
stuff and I'm like, I try to,

00:11:09.569 --> 00:11:11.240
I'm learning how to forgive.

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:12.970
I'm not going to say that I do,

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:14.320
but I'm learning how to forgive

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:16.000
and stuff like that,
you know? (birds chirp)

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:18.640
And I just, man, I just
want to help people in life.

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:19.850
Man, that's all.

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:21.920
You know, because I've done
a lot of bad things too.

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:24.150
And so I didn't do what my father did

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:26.480
but I've done a lot of
others, stupid, stupid things.

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:27.313
You know?

00:11:29.141 --> 00:11:30.034
I don't know.

00:11:30.034 --> 00:11:31.210
(brakes squeal)

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:33.487
I'm by myself now, you know?

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:36.560
I dunno why stuff-

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:39.400
- [Interviewer] So drugs come
into your life at what age?

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:41.650
- About 16 years old.

00:11:41.650 --> 00:11:45.280
You know, I didn't turn to
alcohol like all my uncles

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:47.450
and all that, they died
of cirrhosis of the liver.

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:48.970
I've been to a lot of funerals

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:51.770
and I've seen a lot of, you
know, people turn, you know

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:54.630
when you dyin' of cirrhosis
of the liver, you turn yellow.

00:11:54.630 --> 00:11:56.640
You know, coughing up blood and all that.

00:11:56.640 --> 00:12:00.210
I didn't pick that up, but
I picked up smoking weed,

00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:03.450
doing cocaine, you know,
I tried heroin one time.

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:06.320
No, huh uh, I'm afraid of needles.

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:07.680
- [Interviewer] So your drug is crack?

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:09.200
- Oh yeah, crack cocaine.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:10.570
I still smoke weed, you know.

00:12:10.570 --> 00:12:13.370
I don't drink because
I'm too scared of it.

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:14.480
Plus it's nasty.

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:16.593
I'd rather drink soda, but um,

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:20.394
I'm trying to like stop it, you know?

00:12:20.394 --> 00:12:24.260
I'll like, stay away
from it for a few days,

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:27.300
and then like something
happens, an incident happen.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:28.593
I go right back to it.

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:31.310
I don't know why that is

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:34.010
but I am really trying
to stay away from it

00:12:34.010 --> 00:12:34.843
and stuff like that.

00:12:34.843 --> 00:12:36.860
- [Interviewer] You're surrounded
by it here on skid row.

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:37.693
- Yeah.

00:12:37.693 --> 00:12:38.526
- [Interviewer] You're surrounded
by it. (laughs lightly)

00:12:38.526 --> 00:12:39.480
- Yeah, I know.

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:42.380
But I mean, I could say no
